cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the UK Materials Passport Schema, please cite it as below."
title: "UK Materials Passport Schema (ukmp)"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-11
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Harrison
    given-names: John
    affiliation: "Helix8 Ltd"
  - name: "Helix8 Ltd"
    website: "https://www.materiai.co.uk"
abstract: >-
  An open JSON-LD data format for describing the composition, origin,
  processing history, recycled content, and environmental footprint of a
  material moving between organisations in a circular-economy supply chain.
  Extends the CIRPASS-2 Digital Product Passport framework with UK-specific
  fields, expresses processing history as GS1 EPCIS 2.0 events, and uses the
  W3C Verifiable Credentials v2.0 trust envelope. Work package 1 deliverable
  of the Innovate UK feasibility study "Interoperable Materials Passport
  Infrastructure for UK Circular Economy (Materials 4.0 Focus)".
keywords:
  - materials passport
  - digital product passport
  - circular economy
  - recycled content
  - JSON-LD
  - EPCIS
  - verifiable credentials
  - Materials 4.0
license: Apache-2.0
url: "https://www.materiai.co.uk"
repository-code: "https://github.com/materiAI/ukmp-schema"
identifiers:
  - type: other
    value: "Innovate UK project 10188380"
    description: "National Materials Innovation Programme Feasibility Studies"
